-- Q4480: Terms of Engagement [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Only the auditor, as the party performing the professional services","The auditor and the client''s external legal counsel as co-signatories","Appropriate representatives of both the auditor and the client entity","The auditor, management, and the audit committee chair individually"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under AU-C 210, the engagement letter should be agreed to by appropriate representatives of both the auditor (typically the engagement partner) and the entity (typically management or those charged with governance, as appropriate). Both parties sign to acknowledge and agree to the engagement terms.
Wrong (A): Only the auditor''s signature would be insufficient; AU-C 210 requires agreement from both parties to establish mutual understanding.
Wrong (B): External legal counsel is not a required signatory to the engagement letter under auditing standards.
Wrong (D): While both management and governance may be involved, requiring all three individual signatures is not the standard; "appropriate representatives" of each side suffices.$EXPL$
