-- Q4492: Understanding the Entity and Environment [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["It has no impact because derivatives are considered standard financial instruments","It requires the auditor to withdraw since derivatives are too complex to audit","The auditor should understand the new business line, its accounting, and associated risks","The auditor should rely entirely on management''s representations about the derivatives"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under AU-C 315, when an entity enters a new line of business involving complex transactions like derivatives, the auditor must obtain a thorough understanding of the nature of the transactions, the applicable accounting treatment (including fair value measurement and hedge accounting), and the associated risks. This understanding is essential for identifying risks of material misstatement.
Wrong (A): Derivatives involve significant estimation uncertainty and complexity; dismissing their audit impact would be inappropriate.
Wrong (B): Complexity alone does not require withdrawal; the auditor should obtain the necessary competence or engage a specialist.
Wrong (D): Relying solely on management representations for complex transactions would violate professional skepticism requirements under AU-C 200.$EXPL$
