-- Q4498: Understanding the Entity and Environment [easy/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["They may not be at arm''s length, creating misstatement risks and disclosure requirements","They are always presumed to be fraudulent transactions under auditing standards","The auditor must pre-approve all related party transactions before they occur","They always require the auditor to issue a qualified opinion on the statements"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under AU-C 550, related party transactions may not be conducted at arm''s length and therefore may not reflect fair market values or normal business terms. They create risks of material misstatement because the terms may be unusual, the transactions may lack economic substance, or required disclosures may be omitted.
Wrong (B): Related party transactions are not presumed fraudulent; however, they do require heightened scrutiny due to the risk of non-arm''s-length terms.
Wrong (C): The auditor has no authority to approve or disapprove client transactions; the auditor''s role is to evaluate their effect on the financial statements.
Wrong (D): Related party transactions do not automatically require a qualified opinion; they require proper disclosure and appropriate accounting treatment.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 4498;

